###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/ImperfectInformation
:ImperfectInformation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con210"@en ;
                      rdfs:label "Imperfect Information"@en ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Information which in one or more respects is imprecise, uncertain, incomplete, unreliable, vague or partially true"@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Inclusiveness
:Inclusiveness rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con211"@en ;
               rdfs:label "Inclusiveness"@en ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The principle that AI systems should be designed and used in a way that they are accessible, usable, and beneficial to a diverse range of people, regardless of their age, gender, abilities, or ethnic backgrounds."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/IncrementalLearning
:IncrementalLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
