###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/MechanismDesign
:MechanismDesign rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con274"@en ;
                 rdfs:label "Mechanism Desing"@en ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mechanism design is a subfield of artificial intelligence that focuses on designing systems to achieve specific goals in situations where there are multiple agents or parties involved, each with their own interests and incentives. The tools and lessons of mechanism design are especially useful in auction theory, market design, and social choice theory."@en .


