###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-TaskLearning
:Multi-TaskLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con293"@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Multi-Task Learning"@en ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A subfield of machine learning in which multiple learning tasks are solved at the same time, while exploiting commonalities and differences across tasks."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-agentPlanning
:Multi-agentPlanning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con286"@en ;
                     rdfs:label "Multi-agent Planning"@en ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Planning by (and for) multiple agents. It can involve agents planning for a common goal, an agent coordinating the plans or planning of others, or agents refining their own plans while negotiating over tasks or resources."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-agentSystems
:Multi-agentSystems rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> :Human-MachineInteractionAndCognition ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :ResearchArea ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con287"@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Multi-agent Systems"@en ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Multi-Agent System (MAS) is a type of computer system where multiple independent entities, called agents, work together or compete in a shared environment to reach their goals."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-classLearning
:Multi-classLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con288"@en ;
                     rdfs:label "Multi-class Learning"@en ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In machine learning and statistical classification, multiclass classification or multinomial classification is the problem of classifying instances into one of three or more classes."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-instanceLearning
:Multi-instanceLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con289"@en ;
                        rdfs:label "Multi-instance Learning"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A type of supervised learning. Instead of receiving a set of instances which are individually labeled, the learner receives a set of labeled bags, each containing many instances"@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-labelLearning
:Multi-labelLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con290"@en ;
                     rdfs:label "Multi-label Learning"@en ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Multi-label learning studies the problem where each example is represented by a single instance while associated with a set of labels simultaneously. Multi-label learning  aims to predict multiple labels from a single input data point."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-modalVision
:Multi-modalVision rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con291"@en ;
                   rdfs:label "Multi-modal Vision"@en ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The integration and processing of multiple types of sensory data or input modalities to enhance the understanding and interpretation of visual information."@en .


###  http://aiod.eu/data/schemas/Multi-viewLearning
:Multi-viewLearning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> :Approach ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "con294"@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Multi-view Learning"@en ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A class of machine learning techniques that aims to exploit information from multiple, often complementary, views of the same data."@en .


